spans.s:
प्र-√ लप् P. -लपति, to speak forth (inconsiderately or at random), prattle, talk idly or incoherently, trifle, TBr.; MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to talk, converse, BhP.;
to speak forth, speak, MBh.; Pañcat.;
to exclaim, Bhartṛ.;
to lament, bewail, Pañcat.;
to speak or tell in a doleful manner, MBh.; R.;
to call upon or invoke in piteous tones, MBh. :
Caus. -लापयति, to cause or incite to speak, Mṛcch.

प्र-√ लभ् Ā. -लभते, to lay hold of, seize, MBh.;
to get, obtain, Kathās.;
to overreach, cheat, deceive, befool, MBh.; BhP. :
Caus. -लम्भयति, to cheat, deceive, BhP.

प्र-√ लिख् P. Ā. -लिखति, ˚ते, (P.) to scratch, draw lines in (acc.), Mn. iv, 55;
 to draw lines, write, Hcat.;
 (Ā.) to comb one's head (Sch. ‘to draw lines’), Kauś.; PārGṛ.

प्र-√ लुप् P. -लुम्पति, to pluck or pull out, Hariv. :
Pass. -लुप्यते, to be robbed, MBh.;
to be interrupted or disturbed or violated or destroyed, MW.

प्र-√ लुभ् P. Ā. -लुभ्यति, ˚ते, (Ā.) to lust after, be lustful, follow one's lusts, go astray sexually (said of a wife), ŚāṅkhGṛ.; Mn.;
to allure, entice, seduce, pollute, MBh. :
Caus. -लोभयति, to cause to lust after, allure, entice, attempt, to seduce, MBh.; R.; Pur. &c.;
to divert the attention of any one by (instr.), Suśr.
